  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::56547",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat is likely to interact with Mmp26 through a shared pathway involving matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs). The evidence suggests that Marimastat binds to multiple MMPs, including Mmp23b, Mmp27, and Mmp21, which are all part of the MMP family and participate in the same biological process as Mmp26. This indicates that Marimastat may act as a general inhibitor of MMPs, potentially affecting Mmp26 through a common mechanism. The high scores in all three paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple MMPs in the pathway implies that Marimastat's effect on Mmp26 may be indirect, mediated through the broader MMP signaling network.",
